db/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357470 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357166 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357470 #edb/ref 1069 "q-90720" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357470 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357470 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-7\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6y=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357470 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cb0ac50b-6a2d-5d53-997b-cb65e0ad2bb8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357470 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-7\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+6{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda +6) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda +6=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -6)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =1$ or $\\lambda =6.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{6x}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427565 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186427573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427565 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186427574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427565 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186427575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427565 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427565 #edb/ref 1045 "Second-Order Homogeneous ODEs: Characteristic Equations With Distinct Real Roots" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427565 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186427573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427565 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427565 #e